cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these detection rules in research or writing, please cite them as below."
title: "wrg-sigma-rules"
abstract: >-
  Sigma detection rules for ransomware operators, threat actors, and
  vulnerabilities disclosed in AI/LLM applications and MCP servers, with
  multi-backend conversion (Splunk, Elastic/Kibana, OpenSearch, Wazuh), an MCP
  server, and CI-pinned corpus claims. observed_* rules are derived from a
  specific, cited incident; template_* rules are canonical technique shapes to
  adapt to your own environment.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "WRG-11"
repository-code: "https://github.com/WRG-11/wrg-sigma-rules"
license: MIT
version: 1.11.0
date-released: "2026-09-28"
keywords:
  - sigma-rules
  - detection-engineering
  - detection-as-code
  - threat-detection
  - ransomware
  - mitre-attack
